/**
 * The picture gallery — MTC-FCS-027.
 * ============================================================================
 * A short list of photographs a contractor can drop into an image slot when
 * they have nothing of their own to hand yet. Add a row here and run
 * `npm run gallery`; the script generates the picture, compresses it to AVIF
 * at two sizes and writes both into `static/gallery/`. It skips anything that
 * already exists, so adding the ninth entry costs one image, not nine.
 *
 * ── AVIF, AND A SEPARATE THUMBNAIL ─────────────────────────────────────────
 * The grid shows twenty of these at once. A full-size photograph per tile is
 * megabytes of download to make a decision that needs a hundred pixels, so the
 * thumbnail is what the grid loads and the full file is fetched only when one
 * is chosen. AVIF because these are photographs and it is roughly half of a
 * JPEG at the same quality.
 *
 * ── THEY ARE ILLUSTRATIVE, AND THE UI SAYS SO ──────────────────────────────
 * Stock behind a heading is ordinary; stock in a "gallery of your own work" is
 * a claim about a portfolio that is not true. That is why the premium work
 * gallery takes uploads only and has no stock option at all.
 *
 * `trades` uses the slugs from data/trades.js. An entry that suits everybody
 * — a van, a tool belt, a handshake — takes an empty list and shows under
 * "All" only.
 */

